label TapaniKaarina_grave:
    "... Finally. We're back here."
    "... What a day."
    "It was fascinating to hear what happened to all the others — that there even were others. To meet them."
    "But I've always wondered, naturally."
    "Why weren't they there to raise me?"
    "Auntie never told me the specifics, just that there was an accident."
    "... If dad hadn't died..."
    "I'd have known about all these people."
    v "So... You truly want to find out what happened to them?"
    r "Of course I do! That's why I agreed to help."
    "His eyes get a strange glint in them. It's like he tenses, just a bit."
    v "Very well then. I'll uphold my end of the bargain."
    v "As long as you're ready for what you're about to hear."
    "Despite the sensation of creeping doom hanging in the air, I nod."
    "He reaches out his hand toward the stone."

    v "Tapani Ilvessalo, born 7th of March 1965, and Kaarina Ilvessalo, neé Heikkilä, born 2nd  of June 1970."
    v "Tapani, raised by his father and uncle, grew up fascinated by the skies above."
    v "His studies in meteorology led him to meet Kaarina, a fellow aspiring meteorologist."
    v "They married, and soon after had their first child. Rene."
    v "They kept the baby's name a secret from their respective families — those that they had left. A fun surprise for the christening."
    v "Their lives were happy and ordinary."
    v "One day, on a freezing cold January evening, came a knock at the door."
    v "A strange man stood behind it — old fashioned, four horns atop his head and scales on his cheeks — who proclaimed himself to be Tapani's great grandfather."
    v "He'd been searching for his family for such a long time. Now that he'd finally found someone with his eyes, he just wanted to talk! Catch up a bit."
    v "Tapani, like a fine young gentleman, invited him in for coffee. His hands shook as he poured him a cup."
    v "His great-grandfather, looking but a few years older than him, asked if he knew where the rest of his family had gone. If he's met anyone else with their eyes and tiny horns."
    v "Tapany says: \"I reckon they're all dead. Only knew my dad's side, so don't know much about the rest of the lot.\""
    v "Oh, really now? Well, that's a shame."
    v "What about you? Any children yet?"
    t "Haha, no, not yet. Just me and the wife for now."
    "He lied. An archdemon wouldn't come knocking on their door without a purpose."
    v "Well, that's a relief."
    v "You see, I have this... ailment. An affliction."
    v "Something that cannot be cured, that can't be removed."
    v "And I'll be frank with you — no need to waste both our precious times..."
    v "I'd rather get rid of it."
    v "I have to vacate this body. And yours seems to be in fine shape."
    t "... What? No, wait —"
    t "Is— How would you even do that?!"
    v "I have my ways. Would you like to experience them?"
    v "It'll be painless, I promise! You see, I won't even have to touch you."
    t "P-please, sit back down!"
    v "Just a little flick of the wrist, and I'll open my eyes again, from inside your skull this time. I'll handle the pain, don't worry."
    v "Mind if I borrow one of your knives?"
    t "W-what? No, stop that—!"
    t "Don't!"

    "Tapani and his beloved wife met their swift ends at the claws of a blinded beast, in the burning husk of a newborn home."
    "But there was a sound amidst the creeping heat."
    "The cries of a young baby, echoing from upstairs."
    "A child. Only a few months old. Familiar blood."
    "It would have accommodated him. And it was so small, it didn't even understand its own existence yet."
    "It wouldn't know what it had lost."
    "But the man stumbled out, the baby bundled up in his scarf."
    "A young woman appeared, panicking. Searching for her sister."
    a "Oh my God ... Kaarina?! Kaarina!"
    v "I'm afraid it's too late for them."
    a "Are— Who are you?! Have you called 112?!"
    "The man said nothing. And handed the baby to her."
    a "He's... They didn't—!"
    a "... They didn't even get to name him... God — I don't know his name...!"
    v "... His name would have been Rene."
    "And so the man disappeared into the night, clutching at his eyes that never did quite heal."
    "To lie back down to sleep, to wait until the right time."
    "To search for his living blood once more."

    if p_emp <= 10 and p_rep <= 10 and p_emp >= 5 and p_rep >= 5:
        "...What?"
        r "..."
        r "It was you."
        r "It was your fault."
        v "Yes."
        "It's like all my limbs are  stukc in ice."
        "It's hard to think."
