label Anni_grave:
    r "..."
    r "Well. There she is."
    v "What was her name?"
    r "Anni. Heikkilä. Her husband Jussi is also here."
    v "... Would you like me to...?"
    r "No, it's... I know her story already."
    v "You don't want to hear an outside perspective?"
    r "I'd rather not. It's probably not any different than the one I know."
    v "Well... Mind telling an old man about {i}your{/i} perspective?"
    r "... Anni. Auntie."
    r "I've always lived with her, that's just how it was."
    r "She never pretended that she was my mom, you know. But to me, she was."
    r "Helped me with homework, bandaged up my knees whenever I fell off the bike."
    r "Drove me to the health centre after I fell skating, read me all my favourite bedtime stories whenever I asked."
    r "Sometimes she read her old comics to me and..."
    r "But then I... One summer, I did something."
    v "...?"
    r "I don't think she ever forgave me."
    "I can't stop talking. Why can't I stop talking?"
    "Is it — No it's not. I can stop. I could. {i}But I don't want to."
    r "After that, I didn't really speak with her anymore."
    r "It was like walking on eggshells."
    v "Did she become... unpleasant?"
    r "No. No, she didn't never did. It was worse that she didn't."
    r "And it hurt a lot more. Knowing she didn't mean it anymore."
    r "I knew it. That she hated me for what I'd done."
    r "But even after her and Jussi split up, she let me stay. Bought my laptop and all my upper secondary school books."
    r "I stayed in my room so much, I..."
    r "I didn't initially notice."
    r "She couldn't leave the hospital anymore."
    r "Cancer."
    "..."
    r "I was afraid to go visit her. And then she passed away."
    r "... She probably thought I hated her."
    v "..."
    v "Poor woman."
    r "..."
    v "And you've been on your lonseome ever since?"
    r "Yeah. It's been a few years."
    r "It's been fine."
    v "Has it, now?"

    menu:
        "Not like it's going to get any better.":
            $ p_emp -= 2
            $ p_rep -= 2
            r "... I think this is how it's going to be from now on."
            r "I've gotten used to it."
            r "It'll be fine."
            r "I'm not getting into a university with my grades, or get a job..."
            r "But it'll be fine. Like it always has."
            v "I'm sure you mean that."
            v "... A hopeless case, aren't you?"

        "It hasn't. But it'll get better.":
            $ p_emp += 2
            $ p_rep += 2
            r "... No. It's been like that for so long that it's hard to imagine it any different, you know?"
            r "But... I guess things can change. Maybe if I manage to get a job, or get into univeristy—"
            v "Neither will automatically change anything for the better."
            r "It'd be something, at least."
            v "You've bloomed into quite the optimist, haven't you?"
            r "Not really? I'm just being realistic. Change helps."
            r "Like... Maybe today hasn't been that terrible. It's been pretty interseting, hearing you talk about the past and so on."
            v "Well now! Don't be so open handed with the praise. You don't want people to get used to it."
            r "Just stating facts, that's all."
    v "..."
    v "Your aunt... she was married, right?"
    v "Didn't she have any children of her own?"

    if p_rep >= 6:
        r "..."
        v "... Rene?"
        r "She did."
        r "..."
        "I don't know why he's so interested. He's not related to him at all."
        "But... I get the feeling he won't let me drop the matter now that I've said it."
        r "... Want to meet him?"
        v "Lead the way. If you please."
        jump Elias_grave
    else:
        menu:
            "No.":
                v "... If you insist."
            "No.":
                v "... If you insist."
            "No.":
                v "... If you insist."
        "..."
        r "... So what happened to mom and dad?"
        r "You promised."
        v "Oh, yes. I almost forgot."
        v "Well, get to it. The sun will set before you hear what happened if you just stand there like a doornail."
        jump TapaniKaarina_grave


label Elias_grave:
    r "..."
    v "..."
    v "... So. This is your cousin, I take it?"
    r "Elias."
    r "We... He was more like a brother, though. I knew he wasn't."
    "Why did I come here?"
    r "A bit older than me, so he was always there to kick the shit out of anyone who dared to bully me."
    r "Got into a lot of trouble because of that."
    "It's all flooding back..."
    "And I can't stop."
    "..."
    r "He was a prankster. Put fake spiders in my bed and made me eat rabbit droppings when we were kids."
    r "Then, this one midsummer..."
    #CGs begin
    r "We were at grandparents' cottage."
    r "Me and Elias went swimming. Alone."
    r "I got tired, and sat on the edge of the pier. Dangling my feet in the water. Pretending they were big oars."
    r "I don't know what he thought he was doing, or why..."
    r "But he dove underwater."
    r "It was murky, I couldn't see where he went."
    r "And then I got scared when he didn't come back up."
    r "I thought something had taken him. He just wasn't coming back up."
    r "Something grabbed my ankle."
    r "I didn't— I didn't realise—"
    r "I just kicked on instinct."
    r "... And then I just sat there. Waiting for him to come back up."
    r "I thought he was just pulling a prank on me again."
    r "I sat there, waiting, waiting, and waiting, until I knew he wasn't coming back up. But I had no idea what to do."
    r "..."
    r "...They found his body three days later."
    v "..."
    v "My condolences."
    r "It's alright."
    v "..."
    v "How old were you?"
    r "Ten."
    v "..."
    v "I take it that you think your aunt blamed you for his death?"
    r "I don't 'think' anything, I know it."
    r "Who wouldn't, right?"
    r "My grandparents did, at least."
    v "But it didn't sound like your aunt held any grudged."
    r "She would have kicked me out if she had the heart to. Probably thought she owed it to mom to take care of me."
    v "... Alright then. Maybe she did blame you."
    v "She blamed you for the death of one of her sons, but couldn't bear the idea of losing both."
    r "Stop."
    v "Even if she'd thought that it wasn't an accident,"
    v "She loved you too much to let you suffer because of her."
    r "..."
    r "That's not true. You don't know that."
    v "Are you sure?"

    menu:
        "She didn't love me.":
            $ p_rep -= 5
            r "I know she hated my guts after that."
            r "I know she — that if it had been a choice,"
            r "She would have chosen Elias over me."
            r "I should have drowned in that lake."
            r "And things would have been so much easier. Better."
            r "... Maybe her and Jussi would have stayed together, maybe my grandparents would have still talked to her..."
            r "... I shouldn't be here at all."
            v "..."
            v "{size=-12}If I had known you'd wished for death so badly, I wouldn't have..."
            r "What did you{nw}"
            v "Nothing."
            r "..."
            v "We should go."
            v "... What? Don't just stand there, come along now."
            jump TapaniKaarina_grave

        "... She loved me.":
            $ p_rep += 5
            r "... Yeah."
            r "Yeah, maybe... Maybe she didn't. Hate my guts, I mean."
            r "I dunno, \"love\"'s a strong word."
            v "So is hate."
            r "Guess so."
            r "..."
            r "I wonder why she never asked me to come to the hospital."
            v "Perhaps she thought you'd be better off not seeing her like that."
            v "It can be brutal to see a loved one wither away like that."
            r "... You're not speaking from experience, are you?"
            v "Of course not."
            v "But I, for one, don't doubt that she loved you with all her heart. And if I may be so bold as to guess,"
            v "she'd like you to live a life you're proud of."
            r "..."
            r "We should go."
            v "..."
            r "... What?"
            v "It's nothing."
            v "..."
            r "What are you standing there for? Let's go."
            r "To mom and dad then, right?"
            v "Yes... Yes, I suppose it is that time."
            jump TapaniKaarina_grave

label Neutral_ending:
    "I can't do much else other than watch. My body just refuses to listen."
    "He hesitates for a moment."
    "But his body is lifeless on the ground before I can try and stop him."
    "..."
    "..."
    "Why did he…?"
    "What's happening?"
    "What's happening to me?"
    "Something is. I feel different."
    "I can feel myself changing. I'm slipping away."
    "My hands feel different."
    "I'm sliding down an icy slope and I can't stop myself. There's no end."
    "Endless."
    "Endlessly sliding, slipping, slithering."
    "It's awful. Cruel."
    "Why did he do this to me?"
    "I'm… I'm…"
    "I'm not me…"
    "..."
    "..."
    v "Well, then. What a wholly unpleasant experience."
    v "... Marchosias, you lying hag."
    #Cool ending CG where Valac is walking away in Rene's clothes with his own coat draped over his arm
    return


